        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(durable): add beta3 wake replay foundation",
        "body": "# PR3/5 - wake targets, producers, replay/resume\n\n## Context capsule\n\nThis PR is item 3 of the rebuilt 2026.7.1 beta 3 durable core stack. It is stacked on PR2 and asks reviewers to evaluate the wake target resolver, wake producers, replay attempts, and related schema additions as the next durable-runtime layer.\n\n## Durable core stack overview\n\n- PR1/5 - docs/RFC/boundary anchor and proof plan.\n- PR2/5 - runtime foundation/core plus terminal SQLite row immutability guard.\n- PR3/5 - wake targets, durable producers, replay/resume semantics.\n- PR4/5 - controls/inspection plus CLI/Gateway surface.\n- PR5/5 - internal session delivery handoff, final hardening, and cumulative proof.\n\n## Stack position\n\n- Stack item: PR3/5\n- Current PR summary: Wake target resolver, wake producers, replay attempts, schema additions, targeted replay tests.\n- Does not claim: CLI/Gateway controls, internal session delivery handoff, or plugin SDK DTS size work.\n- Review base / dependency: PR2 head `baa9f679b81092e4bcb435531be661e4fe4d3b43` (`codex/openclaw-durable-beta3-newstack-pr2-runtime-core`)\n- This PR head: `1da730c4031ea430615ba9be8078f5419c82c318` (`codex/openclaw-durable-beta3-newstack-pr3-wake-replay`)\n- Public base branch for GitHub: `release/2026.7.1`\n- Downstream dependency: PR4 depends on this PR.\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nDurable runtime recovery can record pending work, but the runtime also needs a precise way to decide who should be woken, which facts produce wake obligations, and how missed or pending wake delivery attempts are replayed idempotently. This PR adds that layer without adding the later CLI/Gateway controls or internal session delivery handoff.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Parent wake contract store slice.\n- Generalized wake target model and resolver.\n- Wake producers for recorded durable facts.\n- Wake delivery replay attempt ledger, idempotency, and pending-obligation recovery.\n- Durable schema additions and generated shared-state schema/type updates.\n- Focused wake/replay/store/subagent coverage and docs for the wake/attention obligation contract.\n\n## Non-scope\n\n- No CLI/Gateway wake controls or server method surface.\n- No internal session delivery queue handoff.\n- No plugin SDK DTS size fix.\n- No OpenClaw E/service mutation was used for this promotion proof.\n\n## Base / diff hygiene\n\n- Stack ancestry: `git merge-base --is-ancestor baa9f679b81092e4bcb435531be661e4fe4d3b43 HEAD` passed.\n- PR3 slice: 10 commits over PR2, from `d0889dba291` through `1da730c4031`.\n- Changed files vs PR2: 23 files, focused on `src/durable/*`, shared-state schema/type generation, and durable docs.\n- Scope grep for PR4/PR5/plugin SDK surfaces returned no matches:\n  `wake-controls|controls-inspection|wake-internal-delivery|internal-delivery|server-methods|packages/gateway-protocol|src/commands|write-plugin-sdk-entry-dts|plugin-sdk`.\n\n## Proof matrix\n\n| Gate | Command / evidence | Result |\n|---|---|---|\n| PR2 promotion gate | PR2 #104327 live state/head/ClawSweeper check | `OPEN`, `CLEAN`, head `baa9f679b81092e4bcb435531be661e4fe4d3b43`; ClawSweeper overall platinum hermit, proof diamond lobster, patch platinum hermit |\n| Duplicate guard | `gh pr list --head mjnkao:codex/openclaw-durable-beta3-newstack-pr3-wake-replay`; exact-head search | no open PR found before publish |\n| Focused behavior | `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs run --config test/vitest/vitest.unit.config.ts src/durable/wake-target-resolver.test.ts src/durable/wake-producers.test.ts src/durable/wake-delivery-replay.test.ts src/durable/sqlite-store.test.ts src/durable/executor.test.ts src/durable/recovery.test.ts src/durable/subagent.test.ts` | passed, 7 files / 68 tests |\n| Typecheck | `pnpm tsgo:core` | passed |\n| Targeted lint | `node scripts/run-oxlint.mjs ...` over touched durable/state/doc files | passed |\n| Docs map | `pnpm docs:map:gen --check` | passed |\n| Docs inventory | `pnpm docs:list` | passed |\n| Schema/codegen drift | `node scripts/generate-kysely-types.mjs && git diff --exit-code -- src/state/openclaw-state-db.generated.d.ts src/state/openclaw-state-schema.generated.ts src/state/openclaw-state-schema.sql` | passed |\n| Kysely guardrails | `node scripts/check-kysely-guardrails.mjs` | passed |\n| Production dependency/deadcode | `pnpm deadcode:dependencies` | passed after exporting wake replay from the durable runtime barrel |\n| Diff hygiene | `git diff --check baa9f679b81092e4bcb435531be661e4fe4d3b43..HEAD` and working tree diff check | passed |\n\n## Evidence\n\nExact-head local validation for `1da730c4031ea430615ba9be8078f5419c82c318` passed the focused wake/replay behavior suite, core typecheck, targeted lint, docs map/list checks, generated Kysely schema drift check, Kysely guardrails, production dependency/deadcode check, ancestry, diff hygiene, and scope grep. The most relevant behavioral command was:\n\n`node scripts/run-vitest.mjs run --config test/vitest/vitest.unit.config.ts src/durable/wake-target-resolver.test.ts src/durable/wake-producers.test.ts src/durable/wake-delivery-replay.test.ts src/durable/sqlite-store.test.ts src/durable/executor.test.ts src/durable/recovery.test.ts src/durable/subagent.test.ts`\n\nResult: 7 files / 68 tests passed.\n\nThe promotion gate was also rechecked live before submission: PR2 #104327 was open, clean, at `baa9f679b81092e4bcb435531be661e4fe4d3b43`, and ClawSweeper's latest marker for that exact head reported overall platinum hermit, proof diamond lobster, and patch platinum hermit.\n\n## Remote proof note\n\nBlacksmith Testbox through Crabbox was attempted first as the default trusted remote lane, but the environment cannot allocate it because `blacksmith` is not installed in `PATH`:\n\n`node scripts/crabbox-wrapper.mjs warmup --provider blacksmith-testbox --keep --timing-json`\n\nResult: `blacksmith testbox warmup failed: blacksmith failed: exec: \"blacksmith\": executable file not found in $PATH`.\n\nFocused local fallback proof above was run on exact rebased head `1da730c4031ea430615ba9be8078f5419c82c318`.\n\n## Risk / upgrade notes\n\n- Runtime risk: wake routing and replay semantics affect durable recovery behavior and should be reviewed with PR2's opt-in durable runtime contract.\n- Compatibility risk: shared-state schema additions are included and generated artifacts were checked for drift.\n- Product/ownership risk: this remains part of the broader durable runtime stack and inherits PR2's maintainer ownership decision.\n\n## ClawSweeper requirements\n\n- Authored `What Problem This Solves`: yes.\n- Exact-head evidence: yes.\n- Stored data model / migration impact: yes, schema additions are in scope and proof includes generated schema drift checks.\n- Risk labels ClawSweeper should evaluate: compatibility, session-state, message-delivery, durable-runtime, diff-hygiene.\n",
